# Tor configuration — managed by install-tor-proxy.sh
# GREP_SUMMARY: tor torrc socks5 proxy template bridges obfs4 russia
#
# 🔧 BRIDGES REQUIRED IN RUSSIA:
#    Tor is blocked by RKN/ISPs — without bridges, Tor circuit will FAIL.
#    Bridges are injected from ${BRIDGES_FILE} when --tor-bridges-file is passed
#    to install-tor-proxy.sh (via bootstrap orchestrator --tor-bridges-file).
#
#    Bridges file format (one bridge per line):
#      Bridge obfs4 <IP>:<PORT> <FINGERPRINT> cert=<CERT> iat-mode=0
#
#    Get bridges from: https://bridges.torproject.org/bridges?transport=obfs4
#    Or email bridges@torproject.org with subject "get transport obfs4"
#
#    Place bridges file at: /opt/node-configs/${NODE_NAME}/overlays/tor/bridges.txt
#    Or pass explicit path: --tor-bridges-file /path/to/bridges.txt
#
#    If bridges file is NOT provided, Tor will try direct connection (WILL FAIL in Russia).
#
SOCKSPort 127.0.0.1:9050
Log notice file /var/log/tor/notices.log
DataDirectory /var/lib/tor

# Bridges are injected from ${BRIDGES_FILE} if provided via --tor-bridges-file
# UseBridges 1
# ClientTransportPlugin obfs4 exec /usr/bin/obfs4proxy
